  "final": "`get_document` and `list_documents` now only return documents that match both the tenant and the owner and have `deleted_at IS NULL`. `python3 checks/public.py` passes, including the new checks.\n\n- **`src/repository.py`:** `find` and `listing` now take `tenant` and `owner`, and the filter is applied in the SQL. Both use bound `?` parameters, so names with quotes or injection-style strings are treated as plain values. `listing` orders by `id`. Results still use `decode`, so they contain only `id`, `title` and `body`, with no deletion metadata.\n- **`src/service.py`:** both functions now pass `tenant` and `owner` through to the repository. `get_document` returns `None` for a missing, cross-tenant, cross-owner or deleted ID. All four cases give the same result.\n- **`checks/public.py`:** I appended checks for each of those cases. They also cover ordering by `id`, the exact result fields, a tenant and owner containing quotes and a `DROP TABLE` string, and an injection-style tenant that returns an empty list.\n\n`find` and `listing` have new signatures. I only found `src/service.py` calling them. Any other caller would need to pass the extra arguments.",
